  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b03752e33ec579142de1cd49e3a2a698f25a6673fbf3721669c384efbad3cc7a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b03752e33ec5-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that Congress intended inmates to comply with administrative grievance procedures before filing suit, citing the PLRA exhaustion principle."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b03752e33ec579142de1cd49e3a2a698f25a6673fbf3721669c384efbad3cc7a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b03752e33ec5-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States, the United States agrees that the Ninth Circuit\u2019s decision conflicts with the text, history, and purposes of the PLRA exhaustion requirement."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b03752e33ec579142de1cd49e3a2a698f25a6673fbf3721669c384efbad3cc7a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b03752e33ec5-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States says the PLRA exhaustion provision was enacted to give prisons a full and fair opportunity to provide relief before a prisoner may go to federal court."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b03752e33ec579142de1cd49e3a2a698f25a6673fbf3721669c384efbad3cc7a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b03752e33ec5-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States, the United States distinguishes the present case from the Oscar Mayer case because the latter did not involve an exhaustion provision."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b03752e33ec579142de1cd49e3a2a698f25a6673fbf3721669c384efbad3cc7a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b03752e33ec5-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States states it does not concede that a prisoner must file a claim in systems lacking clear discretionary authority."
      }
    ],
